  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\nWe introduce a multi-resolution optimization with adaptive surrogate modeling. The core idea is:\n- Use gradient boosting with overcomplete bases and tensor product feature selection\n- Hybridize with manifold optimization using geodesic flows\n- Incorporate self-supervised initialization from coarse to fine grained solutions\n- Employ block-coordinate descent with adaptive trust regions\n- Maintain adaptive memory of past optima (L2O style)\n\nThe rationale is that standard local methods often underestimate the true global minimum due to:\n- Poor handling of scale-dependent features\n- Rigid initialization away from symmetric candidates\n- Insufficient exploration of multi-modal landscapes\n\nThis mixed-method approach explicitly (a) models the correlation landscape across octaves via tensor decomposition, (b) leverages gradient information only through robust Hessian-aware Jacobians, (c) builds a latent-optima repository for cold-starts, and (d) sequentially unrolls from coarse \u03c7\u00b2 optimization to fine MPC refinement using disciplined convex optimization.\n\nKey original contributions:\n- Overcomplete tensor network initialization\n- Fully distributed geodesic manifold optimization\n- Hessian penalized subspace embedding\n- Multi-stage trust region schemes for interpolation\n\n2. Mathematical Specification:\nGiven domain \u03c3\u00b2=1.0 scaled features, represent solutions via:\nh(n,m) = \u03a3_{k=1}^R a\u2096[m] * exp(-s_k * (|n| + |m|)\u00b2)\n+ Cross terms via tensor constraints\n\nThe optimization cascade consists of:\nPhase I: \u03c7\u00b2 minimization with total correlation +2 regularization\nPhase II: Geodesic averaging over embedded manifolds using Log/Riemannian metrics\nPhase III: Iterative refinement with continuous-time mRNA analogy\n\nThe objective is defined as:\nJ(h) = max_k DSH([h, 1-h], k) \nwith DSH(A,B,k) = \u222bh(x) [1-h(x+k)] dx\n\nConstraints include: \n\u2200k, 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1, \u222bh=1 (discretized by ||h||\u2081 \u2264 \u03c3)\n\nConstraints are enforced via (a) projection operators, (b) barrier functions, and (c) dual variable control. The resulting system is solved via first-order methods with inexact Newton-Krylov acceleration.\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\nTo initialize:\n- Load parent via np.array(initial_h_values, dtype=float)\n- Perform feature transform (if parent available): \u03c3 = parent_std + parent_min\n\nAlgorithm stages:\nI. Tensor-space initialization (50s):\n   h = {}\n   ds = [1.0, 0.75, 0.5, 0.25] # downto\n   for d in ds:\n      n' = n//d\n      h(d) = constrained_SVD(parent, n', T=3)\n      h(d) = normalize_h(h(d), integral=1)\n\nII. Gradient-enhanced manifold climbing (300s):\n   \u03b8 \u2208 \u211d\u1d4f for optimized frequencies\n   \u039b, K = spectral_factors(n)\n   D = double_descent_matrix(h_space=16)\n   H = build_surrogate('GP', n, max_degree=7)\n\nIII. Subspace optimization with trust regions (400s):\n   for \u03bc in [0.7, 0.8, 0.9]:\n      solution = trust_region_lbfgs(J, initial=best_\u03b8, \u03bc=\u03bc)\n      if improvement: augment_features(D, solution)\n      else: coarsen_iter()\n\nIV. Final polishing with MPC problem scaling (200s):\n   Convert to finite control set M\u2081 \n   Reformulate as MPC with LQG penalties\n   Infimal time horizon with exponential discount\n   use[iir forward simulation]\n\nTermination conditions:\n- Relative improvement <: 10\u207b\u2077\n- Time < 1100s\n- No further local valleys\n\n4. Search Choices and Refinements:\nAvailable variations by dictionary mapping:\n\nGA_FEATURE_MAP = {\n    'standard': None,\n    'frequency': {'\u03c9': [6.0, 3.0, 1.5], '\u03a9': [10, 15, 20]},\n    'vector': {'latent': 32, 'compact': True},\n    'geodesic': {'manifold_type': 'rayleigh', 'max_steps':80},\n    'mixed': {'coef': 0.2, 'depth':3}\n}\n\nApplied conditionally by scheduler:\n\ndef adaptive_schedule(time_elapsed, history):\n    if history[-1]['score'] > history[-2]['score']:\n        increase_variations(['frequency', 'mixed'])\n    elif history[-1]['score'] - history[-2]['score'] > 0.001:\n        decrease_variations('vector', '-latent')\n\nActors:\n\nbuffer = deque(maxlen=5)\npast_best = float('inf')\n\ndef update_cadidate(new_score, new_params):\n    buffer.append(new_score)\n    global best_of_run\n    if min(buffer) < past_best:\n        best_of_run = new_score\n        best_params = new_params\n        add_to_repository(best_params)\n\n5. Compute Budget and Timeline:\n\nStaged allocation:\n\ntotal_time = 1100 seconds\n\nStage time allocations:\n\nI.  Initialization: min(100, remaining_time)\nII. Feature space: min(300, remaining_time)\nIII. Adaptive trust region: max(min(500, remaining_time/2, 300), 100)\nIV. Final polishing: min(200, remaining_time)\n\nCheckpoint iterations by exponential moving average of progress.\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract:\n\nOutput validation:\n\nh_values = np.clip(validate_solution(best_h), None, None)\nassert h_values.shape[-1] == target_length, \"Dimension mismatch\"\nassert np.all((h_values>=0) & (h_values<=1)), \"Bounds violation\"\nassert abs(sum(h_values) - n/2.0) < 1e-6, \"Integral failure\"\n\nFinal score:\n\nc5_bound = compute_correlation(h_values, n, log_every=10)\n\nwhere compute_correlation uses:\n\ndef compute_correlation(h, spacing=2.0/n, mode='full'):\n    correlation = np.correlate(h, 1.0-h, mode=mode)\n    return np.max(correlation) * 2.0 / n if mode=='full' else pick_highest(correlation)\n\nThe derived block will use:\n\n- NumPy for basic functionality\n- SciPy.special for interpolation\n- CVXPY for convex subproblems only\n- scikit-learn style Hessian estimators\n- ODE solvers for manifold parts\n\nThe completion returns (h_values, c5_bound, n_points) ensuring:\n\nall((h_values[0] >=0 and h_values[0]<=1)) and similar for other indices\nsum(h_values) \u2248 n/2",
